.TH YAY-LLM-REVIEW 1 "July 2026" "yay-llm-review 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yay-llm-review \- LLM-assisted AUR recipe review companion for yay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yay-llm-review
.IR init | deinit | status | test
.br
.B yay-llm-review scan
.RI [ options ] " package-directory"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Provides an opt-in per-user loader for a yay 13 AURPreInstall Lua hook and
reviews AUR repository files through an OpenAI-compatible llama.cpp server.
It can also manually review an existing AUR checkout. The project is maintained
independently of Arch Linux packaging; an optional Arch package is available
from the AUR. It never modifies user home directories during installation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create the example user configuration and add a managed loader block to yay's
init.lua. The generated configuration remains disabled.
.TP
.B deinit
Remove the managed loader block while retaining the user configuration.
.TP
.B status
Show effective paths and basic configuration.
.TP
.B test
Test the configured llama.cpp server with built-in AUR recipe scenarios. It
checks that the server returns a valid review, allows one benign recipe with a
safe or low risk level, and flags three suspicious recipes: download-and-execute,
disabled checksums, and credential access. It reports each scenario before
sending the request. A suspicious scenario passes for any non-safe risk level,
because the hook warns or blocks on non-safe results regardless of the model's
recommended action. Reviews are sent directly to the server and do not use the
cache. The command exits with 0 when every scenario passes, 1 when a model
classification does not meet the expected result, or 30 when the server cannot
be contacted or returns an invalid response.
.TP
.B test --verbose
Also print the model confidence and all findings for each scenario.
.TP
.B scan
Manually review an AUR checkout. Use --package-base NAME to override its name
and --json to print the normalized model response.
.SH PROGRESS
When standard error is a terminal, the hook displays a spinner while waiting for
llama.cpp. With redirected output it prints one status line. Set
.B show_progress = false
in the configuration to disable this behavior.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/yay/init.lua
Yay Lua configuration containing the managed loader.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/yay-llm-review/config.toml
Per-user scanner configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/yay-llm-review/
Content-addressed review cache.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 allow, 10 warning, 20 block, 30 scanner failure.
.SH SECURITY
This tool is advisory. Keep yay's normal diff review enabled and use isolation
appropriate for untrusted build recipes.
